public class BankAccount {
    private double balance; // hidden — nothing outside can touch it directly

    public BankAccount(double initialBalance) {
        if (initialBalance < 0)
            throw new IllegalArgumentException("Initial balance cannot be negative");
        this.balance = initialBalance;
    }

    // Getter: read-only access from outside
    public double getBalance() {
        return balance;
    }

    // Behavior method: encodes the business rule
    public void deposit(double amount) {
        if (amount <= 0)
            throw new IllegalArgumentException("Deposit amount must be positive");
        balance += amount;
    }

    public void withdraw(double amount) {
        if (amount <= 0)
            throw new IllegalArgumentException("Withdrawal amount must be positive");
        if (amount > balance)
            throw new IllegalStateException("Insufficient funds");
        balance -= amount; // rule checked in ONE place, every time
    }
}

// How callers use it:
BankAccount account = new BankAccount(500.0);
account.deposit(200.0);
account.withdraw(100.0);
System.out.println(account.getBalance()); // 600.0

// account.balance = -500; <-- COMPILE ERROR: balance is private
```
*Switch `balance` from `double` to `BigDecimal` later and not a single caller changes — they all use `getBalance()`, `deposit()`, and `withdraw()`.*

